.TH COOLPING 1 "August 2026" "CoolPing 1.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
coolping \- a stylish, user-friendly alternative to the classic ping command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B coolping
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIhost\fR
.br
.B coolping
\fB--help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
CoolPing provides emoji-based feedback, colorized output, continuous monitoring, and convenient logging, making network diagnostics more fun and informative.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-count N
Number of packets to send (default: 4). N must be a positive integer.
.TP
.B \-\-continuous, \-c
Run indefinitely with a live updating statistics dashboard. Shows real-time metrics including packet loss with a visual bar, an RTT sparkline, latency statistics (current/average/recent/min/max), jitter, connection quality rating, and uptime. Press Ctrl+C to stop.
.TP
.B \-\-log
Enable logging to ~/coolping.log. In continuous mode, state changes and a periodic heartbeat are logged.
.TP
.B \-\-no-emoji
Disable emojis for compatibility with legacy terminals.
.TP
.B \-\-color WHEN
Colorize output: never, always, or auto (default). Colors are also disabled automatically when output is not a terminal or when the NO_COLOR environment variable is set.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose, \-v
Show verbose output including raw ping details.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help message.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B coolping google.com
Basic ping with 4 packets
.TP
.B coolping localhost
Ping a host without a dot in its name
.TP
.B coolping \-\-count=10 google.com
Ping with 10 packets
.TP
.B coolping \-\-continuous google.com
Monitor continuously with live stats dashboard
.TP
.B coolping \-\-continuous \-\-log 8.8.8.8
Continuous monitoring with logging enabled
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Continuous Monitoring
Real-time dashboard showing total pings, success/failure counts, packet loss percentage with a 20-block graph, a sparkline of recent latencies, latency statistics (current, average, recent average, jitter, min, max), connection quality rating (1-5 stars), and an uptime counter.
.TP
.B Quality Ratings
Excellent (<1% loss, <50ms avg), Good (<5% loss, <100ms avg), Fair (<10% loss, <200ms avg), Poor (<25% loss), Bad (everything else).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables color output when set.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on usage errors or when no host is provided.
.SH AUTHOR
Edris Ranjbar
.SH SEE ALSO
ping(8), traceroute(8), mtr(8)
